{
"dur": 83.911,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 9.065,
"text": "Sean collected baseball cards as a boy. In his forties, he fell back in love with the hobby. And in October twenty twenty-four, someone told him about Whatnot.",
"end": 9.34
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 9.34,
"vo_start": 9.615,
"vo_end": 18.695,
"text": "At first it was single cards, maybe a hundred or two a week. It felt like a game on his phone. Then he moved into breaks and unopened packs, and the spending started to climb.",
"end": 18.97
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 18.97,
"vo_start": 19.245,
"vo_end": 27.564,
"text": "Within about three months, he says, his credit cards and personal loans were maxed out. Then a streamer offered him a deal to fill a break, and he reached for his company card.",
"end": 27.839
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 27.839,
"vo_start": 28.114,
"vo_end": 43.593,
"text": "His order emails tell the story. Six dollars. Fourteen. Then four hundred and fifty. Two thousand. Six thousand. And on his last day, twenty-five thousand dollars on a single purchase. No flag.",
"end": 43.868
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 43.868,
"vo_start": 44.143,
"vo_end": 55.543,
"text": "In total, Sean estimates he spent around one point four million dollars on the platform. The cards he won mostly ended up in boxes in his basement. He says the thrill was the process, not the cards.",
"end": 55.818
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 55.818,
"vo_start": 56.093,
"vo_end": 68.211,
"text": "Gambling counsellors call this chasing the dragon: trying to recreate one huge win, however long the odds. And Zachary Kapp, one of those three golden-ticket winners, has said his use spiralled until he checked into rehab.",
"end": 68.486
},
{
"i": 7,
"start": 68.486,
"vo_start": 68.761,
"vo_end": 82.961,
"text": "Another of the three, Kevin Parker, is suing Whatnot, alleging an illegal gambling enterprise. His lawsuit says he spent over ten million dollars and lost about ninety-eight per cent of it. Whatnot wouldn't comment on any individual case.",
"end": 83.911
}
],
